cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use sequential-analysis in your research, please cite it as below.
title: "sequential-analysis: sequential statistical inference separated from the experimental runtime"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Stepanov
    affiliation: Sobolev Institute of Mathematics
  - given-names: Andrej
    family-names: Novikov
    affiliation: Novikov Laboratories LLC
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/andre-a-no/sequential-analysis"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/sequential-analysis/"
abstract: >-
  Sequential statistical procedures (SPRT, Lorden's 2-SPRT, optimal
  Kiefer-Weiss designs, anytime-valid and group sequential tests,
  change-point detection, filtering) written as state-transition functions
  F(S, X, R) -> (S', O, R'), separated from a reproducible runtime with
  checkpoints, replay and conformance vectors. Dual-licensed: GNU AGPL v3,
  or a commercial license from Novikov Laboratories LLC (see COMMERCIAL.md).
keywords:
  - sequential analysis
  - SPRT
  - Kiefer-Weiss problem
  - anytime-valid inference
  - group sequential design
  - change-point detection
  - reproducibility
